WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.825
Unit 3 is the reference architecture,
the first of the guide's six artifacts.

2
00:00:04.825 --> 00:00:06.900
It has seven zones and planes.

3
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:12.250
Managed endpoints carry the Windows client,
Intune policy and the device identity.

4
00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:17.862
Branches send traffic over an I P sec
tunnel, with no user identity on it.

5
00:00:17.862 --> 00:00:22.813
The control plane, Conditional Access,
decides, and never carries traffic.

6
00:00:22.813 --> 00:00:26.968
The policy plane holds the
forwarding and security profiles,

7
00:00:26.968 --> 00:00:29.087
the T L S policies and signaling.

8
00:00:29.087 --> 00:00:31.692
The data plane is
Microsoft's service edge in

9
00:00:31.692 --> 00:00:34.649
commercial Azure regions,
and the provider owns it.

10
00:00:34.649 --> 00:00:39.192
The agency's private network holds
connector groups, private D N S,

11
00:00:39.192 --> 00:00:43.650
applications and domain controller
sensors, all outbound only.

12
00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:47.975
And the evidence zone is the workspace,
Sentinel and the evidence store.

13
00:00:47.975 --> 00:00:52.296
Step 2 makes it the agency's: which
profiles each population gets,

14
00:00:52.296 --> 00:00:57.839
how many connector groups and where, with
two connectors minimum each, the private

15
00:00:57.839 --> 00:01:03.020
D N S suffixes, which branches use remote
networks, and where telemetry lands.
